Typhoon H480 model provenance

The fuselage and propellers were adapted from PX4-SITL_gazebo-classic
at ab7dbc572b4519238f8263ef4a288e6eb80a6076. The author named in model.config
is Lorenz Meier, and the upstream history attributes the original import to
him. The PteroSim adaptation converts the STL files to GLB and adds new
materials, rebuilt skids and a newly modelled battery case.
The gimbal is x500's CGO3: the gimbal model of PX4's gz collection
(Tools/simulation/gz/models/gimbal, by Stefano Colli, Auterion), converted,
welded, shaded smooth and textured as x500's NOTICE describes. That model is
distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License; LICENSE.gimbal holds its text and
copyright notice.

The body is rebuilt from the source's main_body_remeshed_v3.stl as a closed
surface 0.7 mm off it, with its motor pods and shoulder sleeves turned anew
from the source's own profiles, and its shell texture redrawn. Each propeller
hand sits on the rotors that turn its way; the source model mounts its
clockwise blades on the counter-clockwise rotors.

  https://github.com/PX4/PX4-SITL_gazebo-classic/tree/ab7dbc572b4519238f8263ef4a288e6eb80a6076/models/typhoon_h480
