Equipment and mass model

Yuneec's standard Typhoon H specification gives an equipped takeoff
mass of 1.950 kg, a 0.255 kg CGO3+, and the POWER 4 LiPo pack at 4S,
14.8 V nominal, 5400 mAh and 79.9 Wh. The separate stock pack listing
identifies it as YUNTYH105. The installation diagram in the manual
shows how it fits in the bay.

  https://yuneec.kayako.com/en-us/article/2-data-tyhoon-h
  https://yuneec.pl/product-eng-18-Yuneec-YUNTYH105-Typhoon-H-1-Piece-Digital-Camera-Battery-Black.html
  https://yuneec.uk/images/TyphoonHmanuals/TYPHOON-H-USER-MANUAL-V1.1%20LR.pdf

The 0.550 kg installed pack is a modelling estimate. A teardown of the
stock pack reports a 0.527 kg internal assembly with board and connector,
about 125 x 45 x 42 mm; the model allows for the casing and latch. The
camera and battery tensors are cuboid approximations at their fitted
positions. The 1.145 kg remainder includes airframe, drivetrain and
landing gear. Its inertia is scaled from the corresponding Gazebo
links. Component locations and computed CG are simulation estimates.
The generic LiPo open-circuit curve is credited in Batteries/LiPo.xml.
Resistance and avionics draw are simulator settings. The rotor thrust
coefficient comes from Gazebo. Shaft power and reaction torque are
estimated using the static figure of merit of APC's 10x4.5MR model near
the hover RPM. That propeller is a performance reference. The 1000 rad/s
full-command calibration is a simulation estimate. Endurance depends
on that approximation, the manoeuvre and the pack settings.

